The '''Maracaju–Daramazán high speed rail line''', marketed as '''''Viraguaso''''' (from {{Langx|tpn|Uiráwaçu|4=great eagle}}), is a {{convert|1002.08|km|adj=on}} {{W|standard gauge}} {{W|railway line}} that was inaugurated on 9 September 2008. Designed for speeds up to {{convert|380|km/h|mph|0|abbr=on}}. 

Trains are operated by the national [[Baliscan Railways Group]] under the [[AVB]] service.

